projects.description:
The implementation of the WHO Global Initiative for Childhood Cancer in the Philippines specifically aims to: 
1.	Describe the situation and needs for in-country planning and implementation of the technical package (country support plan);
2.	Convene stakeholders across sectors towards shared objectives;
3.	Apply and coordinate four-step approach to scale-up capacity – assess, plan, implement, monitor and modify;
4.	Generate and publish case studies and best practices on childhood cancer control, including assessment reports conducted.
